{"root":{"data":{"id":"42cbe27d2993","created":1645726765,"text":"Machine Learning","expandState":"expand"},"children":[{"data":{"id":"ci4hgsublzk0","created":1645726813333,"text":"Machine\n\nAlgorithms && Models && Data"},"children":[{"data":{"id":"ci4hk1x1n6o0","created":1645727068181,"text":"multiple templates — called algorithms — for machines."},"children":[]},{"data":{"id":"ci4hkm5ojps0","created":1645727112239,"text":"The machines produces from those templates to solve a specific problem are called models"},"children":[]},{"data":{"id":"ci4hl5tzisw0","created":1645727155067,"text":"Models are not 100% correct, but are rather “best guesses” given the amount of data the model has seen"},"children":[]}]},{"data":{"id":"ci4hl8m345k0","created":1645727161120,"text":"Types of \"Learning\""},"children":[{"data":{"id":"ci4hld7a69s0","created":1645727171109,"text":"Supervised Learning"},"children":[{"data":{"id":"ci4hmrhny940","created":1645727280576,"text":"an algorithm needs to see a lot of labeled data examples\ndata that is comprised of both inputs and the corresponding output"},"children":[]},{"data":{"id":"ci4hn54gga80","created":1645727310252,"text":"two classic problems"},"children":[{"data":{"id":"ci4hnde8u7s0","created":1645727328258,"text":"Regression"},"children":[{"data":{"id":"ci9qp7snepk0","created":1646260662569,"text":"Inferring the value of an unknown variable based on other pieces of data that it stands to reason would have an effect on that variable. \nTwo common uses are point in time predictions"},"children":[]}]},{"data":{"id":"ci4jex8mexk0","created":1645732308396,"text":"Classification"},"children":[{"data":{"id":"ci9qqy59axk0","created":1646260798292,"text":"Identifying which category an entity belongs to out of a given set of categories"},"children":[]}]}]}]},{"data":{"id":"ci4hlna8rew0","created":1645727193056,"text":"Unsupervised Learning"},"children":[{"data":{"id":"ci9qrj3d0og0","created":1646260843890,"text":"Clustering"},"children":[{"data":{"id":"ci9qrqvaacg0","created":1646260860816,"text":"Given a certain similarity criteria, find which items are more similar to one another"},"children":[]}]},{"data":{"id":"ci9qrl9djc80","created":1646260848607,"text":"Association"},"children":[{"data":{"id":"ci9qrvjd3ew0","created":1646260870979,"text":"Categorize objects into buckets based on some relationship, so that the presence of one object in a bucket predicts the presence of another."},"children":[]}]},{"data":{"id":"ci9qs72h6400","created":1646260896079,"text":"Anomaly detection. "},"children":[{"data":{"id":"ci9qs9f3bog0","created":1646260901196,"text":"Identifying unexpected patterns in data that need to be flagged and handled. \nStandard applications are fraud detection and health monitoring for complex system"},"children":[]}]}]},{"data":{"id":"ci4hlqu8gd40","created":1645727200795,"text":"Semi-supervised Learning"},"children":[{"data":{"id":"ci9qsmduwt40","created":1646260929419,"text":"This is a hybrid between supervised and unsupervised learning, \nwhere the algorithm requires some training data,\n but a lot less than in the case of supervised learning"},"children":[]}]},{"data":{"id":"ci4hm5j7hbk0","created":1645727232780,"text":"Reinforcement Learning"},"children":[{"data":{"id":"ci9qtbtr6ww0","created":1646260984800,"text":"Here the algorithm starts with a limited set of data and learns as it gets more feedback about its predictions over time."},"children":[]}]}]},{"data":{"id":"ci9qkuwqmr40","created":1646260321062,"text":"Ensemble methods / Ensemble learning "},"children":[{"data":{"id":"ci9qvt4wogw0","created":1646261179208,"text":"the use of multiple models to get a result that is better than what each model could achieve individually. \nThe models could be based on different algorithms or on the same algorithm with different parameters."},"children":[]}]},{"data":{"id":"ci9qxmbyew00","created":1646261321125,"text":"Natural Language Processing(NLP)"},"children":[{"data":{"id":"ci9qy0oz83s0","created":1646261352387,"text":"Keyword generation. Understanding the topic of a body of text and automatically creating keywords for it"},"children":[]},{"data":{"id":"ci9qy5oasgg0","created":1646261363230,"text":"Language disambiguation. Determining the relevant meaning out of multiple possible interpretations of a word or a sentence"},"children":[]},{"data":{"id":"ci9qybx8zog0","created":1646261376832,"text":"Sentiment analysis. Understanding where on the scale of negative to positive the sentiment expressed in a text lies"},"children":[]},{"data":{"id":"ci9qyi1jw540","created":1646261390153,"text":"Named entity extraction. Identifying companies, people, places, brands etc. in a text; \nthis is particularly difficult when the names are not distinctive"},"children":[]}]},{"data":{"id":"ci9qzp0pbls0","created":1646261483703,"text":"Problem Affects the Solution"},"children":[{"data":{"id":"ci9qztrb8bc0","created":1646261494019,"text":"Algorithm Selection"},"children":[{"data":{"id":"ci9r14s34js0","created":1646261596375,"text":"A small change in the problem definition could mean a completely different algorithm is required to solve it, or at a minimum a different model will be built with different data inputs."},"children":[]}]},{"data":{"id":"ci9qzyhj5k00","created":1646261504312,"text":"Feature Selection"},"children":[{"data":{"id":"ci9r0vhzjqo0","created":1646261576173,"text":"ML models identify patterns in data. \nThe data you feed into the models is organized into features (also called variables or attributes)"},"children":[]}]},{"data":{"id":"ci9r018hn3c0","created":1646261510295,"text":"Objective Function Selection"},"children":[{"data":{"id":"ci9r0ktiy5c0","created":1646261552926,"text":"The objective function is the goal you're optimizing for or the outcome the model is trying to predict."},"children":[]}]},{"data":{"id":"ci9r08bcbwo0","created":1646261525705,"text":"Explainability and Interpretability"},"children":[{"data":{"id":"ci9r3gk03j40","created":1646261778736,"text":"The output of ML models is often a number — a probability, a prediction of the likelihood something will happen or is true."},"children":[]}]}]},{"data":{"id":"ci9r40a38yw0","created":1646261821672,"text":"Modeling and Performance \nMeasurement Pitfalls"},"children":[{"data":{"id":"ci9r7trx9ls0","created":1646262120970,"text":"Overfitting"},"children":[{"data":{"id":"ci9r8anpu680","created":1646262157721,"text":"the accuracy of the model on the data you train it with is significantly better than its accuracy on the data with which you validate and test"},"children":[]}]},{"data":{"id":"ci9ra07oqu00","created":1646262291712,"text":"Precision, Recall and the tradeoff Between Them"},"children":[{"data":{"id":"ci9rago1d9c0","created":1646262327529,"text":"Precision measures the share of true positive predictions out of all the positive predictions the algorithm generated"},"children":[]},{"data":{"id":"ci9rc1cac2o0","created":1646262450895,"text":"Recall is the share of positive predictions out of all the true positives in the data"},"children":[]}]}]},{"data":{"id":"ci9rlq8lvjc0","created":1646263210370,"text":"Modeling","hyperlink":"https://medium.com/@yaelg/product-manager-guide-part-3-developing-a-machine-learning-model-from-start-to-finish-c3e12fd835e4","hyperlinkTitle":"Developing a Machine Learning Model from Start to Finish"},"children":[{"data":{"id":"ci9rlzp5wps0","created":1646263230962,"text":"Ideation"},"children":[{"data":{"id":"cian4c137zk0","created":1646352122766,"text":"Align on the problem"},"children":[]},{"data":{"id":"cian4g4laa00","created":1646352131685,"text":"Choose an objective function"},"children":[]},{"data":{"id":"cian4kc251k0","created":1646352140844,"text":"Define quality metrics"},"children":[]},{"data":{"id":"cian4r79rag0","created":1646352155792,"text":"Brainstorm potential inputs"},"children":[]}]},{"data":{"id":"ci9rm7uwihs0","created":1646263248724,"text":"Data Preparation"},"children":[{"data":{"id":"cian4xg31uo0","created":1646352169385,"text":"Collect data for your prototype in the fastest way possible"},"children":[]},{"data":{"id":"cian5kz2hew0","created":1646352220599,"text":"Data cleanup and normalization"},"children":[]}]},{"data":{"id":"ci9rmex8wvk0","created":1646263264102,"text":"Prototyping and testing"},"children":[{"data":{"id":"cian5og3fdk0","created":1646352228159,"text":"Build prototype"},"children":[]},{"data":{"id":"cian5vaiwew0","created":1646352243060,"text":"Validate and test prototype"},"children":[]},{"data":{"id":"cian5zz453k0","created":1646352253254,"text":"Iterate"},"children":[]}]},{"data":{"id":"cian3ynvk9c0","created":1646352093669,"text":"Productization"},"children":[{"data":{"id":"cian6622qw00","created":1646352266494,"text":"Increase data coverage"},"children":[]},{"data":{"id":"cian6a0ptwg0","created":1646352275119,"text":"Scale data collection"},"children":[]},{"data":{"id":"cian6dagu4g0","created":1646352282238,"text":"Refresh data"},"children":[]},{"data":{"id":"cian6h0eiqo0","created":1646352290337,"text":"Scale models"},"children":[]},{"data":{"id":"cian6kp2uwg0","created":1646352298359,"text":"Check for outliers"},"children":[]}]}]}]},"template":"right","theme":"fresh-blue","version":"1.4.43"}